CloudBurrow patch 29 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1273). Applies after patch 0028.

The gap: BigQuery keeps a streaming buffer for a table partitioned by a
column too: rows streamed by tabledata.insertAll are read by queries at
once, but sit in the __UNPARTITIONED__ partition until BigQuery extracts
them, are not counted in the table's numRows, are not copied, and cannot
be changed by DML (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/streaming-data-into-bigquery,
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/data-manipulation-language#limitations).
Unlike an ingestion-time partitioned table's, whose buffered rows have
_PARTITIONTIME NULL (patch 0028), such a table has no column that tells
a buffered row from the others.

The patch gives a CREATE TABLE with a column list and a PARTITION BY that
is not ingestion time the column _PARTITION_BUFFERED BOOL, a pseudo-column
as patch 0028 makes _PARTITIONTIME one: SELECT * leaves it out, an INSERT
may give it and a query names it. CloudBurrow's front sets it TRUE on a
streamed row and NULL when the buffer flushes. BigQuery reserves the
column-name prefix _PARTITION, so no column of a table can be named so.
streaming_buffer_mark_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

